.git
.venv
# Installed inside the build from the lockfile, never copied in. Without this the console's
# host `node_modules` travels into the build context, which is hundreds of megabytes of files
# the build immediately overwrites, and any native module in it is built for the wrong
# platform.
**/node_modules
# Built inside the build too. A host bundle copied in would be overwritten by `npm run build`
# in the console stage, and silently shipped by anything that ever skipped that step.
console/dist
__pycache__
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
tests
ops
# The one file out of `ops` the image needs: the identity realm, which the Keycloak stack
# imports and which cannot be bind-mounted where this is deployed. Everything else in `ops`
# is runbooks and host scripts with no business in a container that serves requests, so the
# exclusion above stays and this is a hole in it rather than a change of mind.
!ops/keycloak/realm-export.json
docs/wbs
*.md
!README.md
